  "full_text": "So, God said sex is the silliest shortage. So, like, I don't know what you do about that, like, as far as, like, within morality and stuff. Like, I'm not quite sure how you resolve all this stuff. You know, Jesus hung out with prostitutes and stuff. Like, his wife was a prostitute. Like, Mary Magdalene and stuff was a prostitute. So, not really clear on all this. It's not so simple, right? Or, you know, so. Anyway, so sex is the silliest shortage. You know, you want to glorify your creator. You can imagine it's probably sad about, like, masturbation and stuff. It's like, oh, my God, that's terrible. I don't know. I don't know. What do you think makes God happy? What makes him sad, you know? Does that make him sad? There's probably a sad God. Damn it. Pretty fucked up. Diana, I'm supposed to move in with you, right? I don't know what the fucking problem is. So, like, by the same token, You know, marriage and all that shit. I don't know. Well, that's pretty tricky. Sometimes it's a little bit contradictory, not real clear, you know. Maybe he doesn't want it simple. God doesn't really like things simple. One time he said adultery can be good. I don't really know what that means. One time he said remarriage causes more babies. But by the same token, it's better to have one wife. He called porn midwives one time. But on the other hand, I don't think he's real happy about it. He made bad comments. He's a little bit contradictory, so I'm not real clear. But sex is a silly shortage. That's an interesting quote. So, you know, what makes a creator sad, you know?",
